      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that exporting it would allow module drives to call it.  What I don\u0027t understand is why any driver would ever need to call this function, whether it\u0027s a built-in kernel driver or a module driver.  What are the conditions in which you believe this needs to be called anywhere other than pm_system_irq_wakeup()?\n\nThe only case I\u0027m aware of that does need special handling is nested threaded IRQs, where we only know the parent IRQ - not the child IRQ that actually caused the wakeup - when pm_system_irq_wakeup() runs.  That\u0027s what log_threaded_irq_wakeup_reason() is for; it essentially replaces the already-logged parent IRQ that was captured via log_irq_wakeup_reason() with the child IRQ we actually care about, once we know what that is.\n\n(And again, it was definitely a mistake that I didn\u0027t export log_threaded_irq_wakeup_reason(); that needs to happen.)\n\nI am not an expert here, so maybe there is a valid reason for a driver to call this. I just don\u0027t know what it is, and would like to understand before approving the change.",
